{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QTBkGwsZsMywM7ojrK5GV9","type":"tool_result","content":"/* vsmemo: rule-free exact decision \"vertex separation (= pathwidth) <= w?\".\n   Written from scratch 2026-10-12; shares no code with the project's searches.\n\n   Search over layout prefixes S (vertex sets). A prefix is admissible iff its\n   inner boundary {v in S : v has a neighbour outside S} has at most w vertices.\n   pw <= w iff the full set is reachable from the empty set through admissible\n   sets adding one vertex at a time. Depth-first search; every set found not to\n   reach the full set is stored in a hash table (the only pruning: whether the\n   full set is reachable from S depends on S alone). No dominance rule, no bound.\n\n   Optional -f (off by default): add at once a vertex v outside S with N(v)\n   contained in S. Sound: moving such a v to directly after S in any layout\n   does not enlarge any later prefix boundary (v contributes nothing to it and\n   leaving it outside could only add its neighbours to the boundary).\n\n   Optional -o: use the outer boundary |N(S) - S| of each prefix instead. The\n   maximum over a layout's prefixes of the outer boundary equals the maximum of\n   the inner boundary over the reversed layout's prefixes (the outer boundary of\n   P is the inner boundary of V - P), so both decide the same question; they\n   differ only in which sets the search visits. -f also holds under -o (v leaves the outer boundary, N(v) adds nothing).\n\n   -w FILE (with UNSAT, without -f): write every stored prefix. They form a\n   family F with the empty set in F, the full set not in F, and every admissible\n   one-vertex extension of a member again a member, which is what checkF verifies.\n\n   usage: vsmemo EDGES.txt W [-f] [-o] [-t SECONDS] [-m MAXSTATES] [-w FILE]\n   EDGES.txt: first line \"n m\", then m lines \"u v\" (0-based).\n   prints \"SAT order ...\" / \"UNSAT\" / \"UNKNOWN\" and the number of states. */\n#include <stdio.h>\n#include <stdlib.h>\n#include <string.h>\n#include <stdint.h>\n#include <time.h>\n\n#define W 3\ntypedef struct { uint64_t w[W]; } set_t;\nstatic int n, wmax, forced = 0;\nstatic set_t nb[192], full;\nstatic uint64_t states = 0, maxstates = 2000000000ULL;\nstatic double deadline = 1e18;\n26:   usage: vsmemo EDGES.txt W [-f] [-o] [-t SECONDS] [-m MAXSTATES] [-w FILE]\n113:int main(int argc, char **argv) {\n114:    if (argc < 3) { fprintf(stderr, \"usage: vsmemo EDGES W [-f] [-t SEC] [-m MAXSTATES]\\n\"); return 2; }\n115:    FILE *f = fopen(argv[1], \"r\"); int m;\n118:    wmax = atoi(argv[2]);\n120:        if (!strcmp(argv[i], \"-f\")) forced = 1;\n121:        else if (!strcmp(argv[i], \"-o\")) outer = 1;\n122:        else if (!strcmp(argv[i], \"-t\")) deadline = now() + atof(argv[++i]);\n123:        else if (!strcmp(argv[i], \"-m\")) maxstates = strtoull(argv[++i], 0, 10);\n124:        else if (!strcmp(argv[i], \"-w\")) dump = argv[++i];\n/* checkF: checks a refutation certificate of \"vertex separation <= w\"\n   (outer-boundary form), independently of the search that produced it.\n   Input: EDGES.txt (\"n m\" then m lines \"u v\", 0-based), w, and a file of\n   vertex sets, ceil(n/8) bytes each (bit v of byte v/8 = vertex v).\n   Checks: (1) the empty set is in F; (2) the full vertex set is not in F;\n   (3) for every S in F and every v not in S with |N(S+v) - (S+v)| <= w,\n   S+v is in F. Then no layout has every prefix boundary <= w: its prefixes\n   start in F (1), stay in F (3), and would end at the full set, contradicting (2).\n   Prints VERIFIED or the first failure.  usage: checkF EDGES.txt W FILE */\n#include <stdio.h>\n#include <stdlib.h>\n#include <string.h>\n#include <stdint.h>\nstatic int n, B;\nstatic unsigned char *F; static size_t cnt;\nstatic int cmp(const void *a, const void *b) { return memcmp(a, b, B); }\nstatic int in(const unsigned char *s) { return bsearch(s, F, cnt, B, cmp) != NULL; }\nstatic int bit(const unsigned char *s, int v) { return s[v >> 3] >> (v & 7) & 1; }\nint main(int argc, char **argv) {\n    if (argc != 4) { fprintf(stderr, \"usage: checkF EDGES W FILE\\n\"); return 2; }\n    FILE *f = fopen(argv[1], \"r\"); int m; if (fscanf(f, \"%d %d\", &n, &m) != 2) return 2;\n    B = (n + 7) / 8;\n    unsigned char (*adj)[256] = calloc(n, 256);\n    for (int i = 0; i < m; i++) { int u, v; if (fscanf(f, \"%d %d\", &u, &v) != 2) return 2; if (u != v) adj[u][v] = adj[v][u] = 1; }\n    int w = atoi(argv[2]);\n    FILE *g = fopen(argv[3], \"rb\"); fseek(g, 0, SEEK_END); long sz = ftell(g); fseek(g, 0, SEEK_SET);\n    if (sz % B) { printf(\"bad file size\\n\"); return 1; }\n    cnt = sz / B; F = malloc(sz); if (fread(F, 1, sz, g) != (size_t)sz) return 2;\n    qsort(F, cnt, B, cmp);\n    for (size_t i = 0; i + 1 < cnt; i++) if (!memcmp(F + i * B, F + (i + 1) * B, B)) { printf(\"duplicate set\\n\"); return 1; }\n9:   Prints VERIFIED or the first failure.  usage: checkF EDGES.txt W FILE */\n19:int main(int argc, char **argv) {\n20:    if (argc != 4) { fprintf(stderr, \"usage: checkF EDGES W FILE\\n\"); return 2; }\n21:    FILE *f = fopen(argv[1], \"r\"); int m; if (fscanf(f, \"%d %d\", &n, &m) != 2) return 2;\n25:    int w = atoi(argv[2]);\n26:    FILE *g = fopen(argv[3], \"rb\"); fseek(g, 0, SEEK_END); long sz = ftell(g); fseek(g, 0, SEEK_SET);\n29:| myciel6: pw >= 38 | 58 / 691 (min-d) | rule-free search + checkF | 0.02 s search, 0.02 s check | 24,321 sets, 195 KB raw, 64 KB xz (kept) | **certified** |\n30:| myciel6: pw >= 38 | 60 / 693 (min-d) | rule-free search + checkF | 0.04 s, 0.06 s | 46,620 sets, 373 KB raw, 128 KB xz (kept) | **certified** |\n32:| myciel7: pw >= 71 | 110 / 2,198 (min-d) | rule-free search + checkF | 3.7 s, 6.5 s | 3,398,378 sets, 47.6 MB raw, 13.2 MB xz (kept) | **certified** |\n33:| Random-125-125-2-3_0: MOSP >= 21 (pw >= 20) | 70 / 250 (least-c) | rule-free search + checkF | 2.8 s, 4.4 s | 2,698,884 sets, 24.3 MB raw, 10.3 MB xz (kept) | **certified** |\n35:| Random-125-125-2-1_0: MOSP >= 24 (pw >= 23) | 87 / 311 (min-d) | rule-free search + checkF | 255 s (19.7 GB RAM), 249 s | 139,289,255 sets, 1.53 GB raw; not kept (xz > 50 MB) | **certified** |\n37:| Random-125-125-6-1_0: MOSP >= 81 (pw >= 80) | 120 / 2,079 (min-d) | rule-free search + checkF | 39 s, 81 s | 23,576,438 sets, 354 MB raw, 102 MB xz; not kept | **certified** |\n38:| SP4: MOSP >= 53 (pw >= 52) | 96 / 1,037 (min-d) | rule-free search + checkF | 17 s, 22 s | 11,415,333 sets, 137 MB raw, 44.3 MB xz (kept) | **certified** |\n64:- the checker `checkF.c`, 80 lines, which replaces trust in the search;\n89:- **The inner-boundary search form is much slower.** `vsmemo` was first run\n170:`vsmemo.c` decides `pathwidth(H) <= w` by depth-first search over layout\n180:On UNSAT, `-w` writes the stored family `F`. `checkF.c` reads the graph, `w` and\n196:- `mc_vsmemo_test.py`: 1,500 random graphs to 13 vertices, at `pw - 2 .. pw`,\n198:- `mc_checkF_test.py`: 365 genuine certificates verify. Each with one set\n252:gcc -O2 -march=native -o vsmemo vsmemo.c\n253:gcc -O2 -o checkF checkF.c\n257:python mc_vsmemo_test.py                  # vsmemo against brute force\n258:python mc_checkF_test.py                  # checkF accepts genuine, rejects damaged certificates\n273:xz -dk proofs/myciel7_m110_w70.F.xz && ./checkF myciel7_m110_edges.txt 70 proofs/myciel7_m110_w70.F\n276:./vsmemo myciel7_m110_edges.txt 71 -o\n285:./vsmemo myciel7_full_edges.txt 72 -o     # a width-72 layout","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9f928aeb-dd8b-4eb2-ae60-0ddf3b071136","uuid":"43635d3b-3190-44a4-b0d4-8ce9fd7515e1","timestamp":"2026-11-03T03:26:58.284Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"/* vsmemo: rule-free exact decision \"vertex separation (= pathwidth) <= w?\".\n   Written from scratch 2026-10-12; shares no code with the project's searches.\n\n   Search over layout prefixes S (vertex sets). A prefix is admissible iff its\n   inner boundary {v in S : v has a neighbour 