asures the record and freezes the targets. Items 02–03 are family E (the ceiling by search, the exact floor by branch and bound and by SAT with DRAT). Items 04–05 are family M (the contraction-sequence search, its certificate and checker, the 338 and the 200 Chu & Stuckey, the two ridge instances). Item 06 is family B with certified branches. Item 07 is the 24 open classes, after the searches are validated on known optima (the tree first, on paper). Item 08 draws the duality-gap map and states the kill verdicts. Item 09 is Lean. Item 10 writes; 11 is the reserve.  ## Target Problems (in order) See `iterations.md`. Work on exactly ONE unchecked item per iteration; the item's full text is in the prompt and in the file. An item that depends on a blocked (`- [!]`) item uses what the record has (item 01's `floor0`, the ladder as the M floor) and says so.  ## Acceptance Criteria (per item) - [ ] The deliverable exists where the item says, states its size range,       gives its regenerate command, has a kill verdict (met / not met /       none), and says what it does not claim. - [ ] New code has tests under `tests/`; new Lean has no `sorry` and no       `axiom`, is imported by `lean/MOSPFormalization.lean`, and every new       theorem has a `#print axioms` line in `paper1/axiom_check.lean`. - [ ] Every certificate the report cites has been run through       `paper1/obstruction_check.py` and the verdict is in the item's CSV. - [ ] Every floor the item produces has been through       `learning/bound_harness.py`'s validity stage on its instances       (\"above optimum\" must be 0) or the item says why not. - [ ] `python3 Ralph_Loops/loop0013/gate.py` passes (lake build, imports,       sorry and axiom count at zero, MOSP pytest about 5 min,       pathwidth_solver pytest about 7 min, `make -C paper1/latex check`).       Run `make -C paper1/latex` before the gate if the PDF is stale. - [ ] A section appended to `reports/obstruction_search.md` (create it in       item 01), and a