h: the contraction-sequence search, its certificate and checker; the 338 at `n ≤ 60` against the greedy ladder (item 04)","+","+*Size range: the 251 instances of `gap338` with at most 60 customers (in","+fact 20–50: the set has nothing at 51–60); validation on 50 corpus instances","+at `n ≤ 16` and on the six certificates of","+`reports/minor_bound_verification.md` (58–120-vertex minors). Regenerate:","+`nice -n 19 python3 -m learning.obstruction_minor --stage validate`;","+`nice -n 19 python3 -m learning.obstruction_minor --stage run --targets","+gap338 --max-n 60 --workers 8 --seconds 60,120`; `--stage check --workers 8`","+(every certificate through the independent checker, rule-free included);","+`python3 reports/scratch/obstruction_search/04_minor/run_harness.py","+--workers 8` (the validity stage); `--stage tables`; `python3","+paper1/obstruction_check.py check-minor <instance.mosp> <certificate.json>`","+on any one certificate. Outputs under","+`reports/scratch/obstruction_search/04_minor/`: `search.csv` (251 rows, the","+ladder's and the search's result per instance), `ladder.csv` (2,155 ladder","+points), `joined.csv`, `certificates/<instance>/{instance.mosp, search.json,","+ladder.json, ladder_points.json}`, `checker_verdicts.csv`, `validation.log`,","+`validation_small.csv`, `validation_recorded.csv`, `validation_recorded/`,","+`harness_values.csv`, `harness_table.md`, `tables.md`, `run.log`, the three","+`check_attempt*.out` of §4.1, and `../04_minor_{validate,run,check}.out`.","+Tests: `tests/test_obstruction_minor.py` (11).*","+","+### 4.1 What was done","+","+**The question.** Family M is the one obstruction family on record that","+reaches the ridge instances (item 01: minors close 4 of the 5","+`Random-125-125-2` instances) and the one that is a genuine maximisation","+(plan §0.2): any contraction minor `H` of the MOSP graph with a proved","+pathwidth `p` certifies `MOSP ≥ p + 1`, by minor monotonicity","+(`pathwidth_gt_of_minorOf`, `lean/MOSPFormalization/Minor.lean`) and","+`mospValue_eq_pathwidth_add_one`. What is on record is the *greedy ladder*","+(`satisfiability/relaxation.py::minor_sequence`, the C program's own minor","+step): two contraction rules (`min-d`, `least-c`), fixed sizes, a refutation","+attempted on each. This item asks whether a local search over contraction","+*sequences* finds minors the ladder misses, at equal caps and equal total","+time; what the family's duality gap is on the 338 at `n ≤ 60`; and what a","+minimal certifying minor looks like.","+","+**The search** (`learning/obstruction_minor.py`, plan §0.5 (e)). The state","+is a sequence of `(v, u)` pairs in the instance's customer labels (contract","+`v` into `u`; `(v, −1)` deletes an isolated `v`), replayed by `replay`, which","+mirrors `relaxation.minor_groups`'s checks on masks (every pair an edge of","+the current graph, a deletion only of an isolated vertex) and raises on any","+violation. Moves: delete a pair (the minor grows by a vertex), insert a pair","+(an edge of the current minor), retarget a pair to another current","+neighbour of `v`, move a pair earlier; the result goes through `repair`","+(a dead `v` drops the pair, a `u` no longer adjacent is retargeted to `v`'s","+current neighbour of least degree, a `v` left with no neighbour becomes a","+deletion). Tabu tenure 10 on the absorbed vertex, with aspiration; restarts","+cycle through the two greedy rules at 50, 60, 70, 80, 90 and 95% and the","+incumbent, 25 moves each; plateau moves are accepted (equal floor, at most","+one vertex larger). **Evaluation** of a candidate minor `H`: the certified","+witness's opening layout lifted to `H` (each branch set at its first","+member's position; a proof that the lifted layout's vertex separation never","+exceeds the original's is in `lifted_layout`'s docstring and the inequality","+is asserted on 300 random graphs by a test) and a greedy layout give an","+upper bound on `pw(H)`; a candidate whose upper bound cannot improve the","+best floor so far is not sent to the C program (a cache by edge hash","+removes repeats); otherwise one call","+`printf '%s\\n' \"$g6\" | nice -n 19 pathwidth_solver/cli/pathwidth -t 2 -l -v -m min_vertices=1000000`","+(graph6 by networkx, labels `0..m−1` in increasing order of the surviving","+representative; the C's own minor step disabled, so the certificate is","+ours), parsed for `pathwidth <w> <status>` and stderr's `lower=`: the floor","+certified is `w + 1` on `refutation` or `bound`, `lower + 1` on `upper`.","+The objective is the certified floor in optimum units, ties by fewer","+vertices. **The baseline** is the ladder — both rules, 50–85% in 5% steps","+then 90 and 95% — through the same evaluator at the same cap; it stops","+when its floor reaches the optimum (its points come in increasing size, so","+the first is its smallest certifying point). Both get the same budget per","+instance, 60 s at `n ≤ 40` and 120 s at 41–60; the search runs its whole","+budget, minimising the vertex count once at the optimum. The C binary's","+SHA-256 (`6560b809…`) is in every certificate.","+","+**The certificate** (`certificates/<instance>/search.json`, format","+`obstruction-minor-1`): instance name, `n`, the SHA-256 of the rows and of","+`G`'s edge list, the sequence, `m`, the minor's labels, edges and edge hash","+(the contract: SHA-256 of `\"m e\\n\"` then one `\"a b\\n\"` per sorted edge),","+the C's width, status and `lower`, the pathwidth proved and the width","+refuted, the C's stdout and stderr verbatim, its binary's SHA-256, the cap,","+the seconds, and the theorems. The ladder's best point is written beside it","+as `ladder.json`, with every ladder point in `ladder_points.json`.","+","+**The checker** (`paper1/obstruction_check.py check-minor`; imports nothing","+from `learning/`, `satisfiability/`, `pathwidth_solver/`, `mosp/` or","+networkx — a test pins this): its own `.mosp` and edge-list readers, its own","+MOSP graph, its own contraction replay (dict-of-sets, as `mc_graph.py`),","+the quotient rebuilt from the branch sets and compared with the replayed","+minor, the edge hash compared with the certificate's, its own graph6","+encoder (equal to networkx's on 300 random graphs, by a test), the C program","+re-run on the minor at the cap ×5 and accepted only if it proves at least","+the claimed pathwidth, and, where `m ≤ 80`, `vsmemo.c` and `checkF.c` from","+`reports/scratch/minor_certificates/` compiled into a temporary directory","+and run for a rule-free refutation of `claim − 1` (`vsmemo -o -w F`, cap","+300 s, 10⁸ states, an 8 GB address-space limit) with `checkF` on the family","+of sets. The verdict is `verified` when replay, hash and C agree; the","+rule-free outcome (`verified` / `unknown` / `skipped` / `failed` / `sat`)","+is recorded beside it, and a `sat` or `failed` rejects.","+","+**Validation before the 338** (`validation.log`). (i) 50 corpus instances","+at `n ≤ 16` (seed 0 from `targets.small`): every ladder point with the skip","+disabled and every minor the search proposed in 10 s — **1,485 distinct","+minors, 1,485 C calls** — compared with","+`learning.first_moment.vertex_separation_brute`: **0 disagreements**. (ii)","+The six recorded certificates (`Random-125-125-2-3_0` m70, `2-1_0` m87,","+`6-1_0` m120, `SP4` m96, `myciel6` m58, `myciel7` m110), converted from","+`mc_graph.py`'s `[keep, absorbed]` convention to this item's `[absorbed,","+keep]` and run through the checker with the C at 60 s: **6 of 6 replay,","+6 of 6 hash-match, 6 of 6 re-proved by the C at exactly the recorded","+width** (statuses all `refutation`; 0.03–28 s, the 87-vertex minor the","+slowest). The rule-free check was not repeated on them (they are","+rule-free certified on record).","+","+**The run** (`run.log`). 251 instances, started at 8 workers under a","+one-minute load of 2.4; after 74 instances the load rose to 48–59 from the","+owner's chrome/puppeteer processes and the run was stopped and resumed at 4","+workers (the stage resumes by instance name; the in-progress instances were","+redone), then at 8 again when the load fell to 4 after 114. The search's","+budgets are wall-clock, so the instances run under load got fewer moves per","+second; nothing else changes. Wall 1,084 + 604 + 1,015 s in the three","+segments.","+","+**Three checker attempts, two bugs in the checker, none in a certificate**","+(`check_attempt{1,2,3}.out`). The first sweep crashed with \"branch sets do","+not partition the vertex set\": the checker's partition check ignored","+isolated-vertex deletions. The second, counting the deleted vertex, still","+rejected 5 certificates (`p1540n3_0`, `p1550n8_0`, `p2050n4_0`, `p2550n4_0`,","+`p2550n5_0`): in each, a whole component (a 4-customer pattern clique, e.g.","+`{9, 14, 23, 37}` of `p1540n3_0`) had been contracted to one vertex and","+*then* deleted as isolated — a valid minor operation that deletes the whole","+branch set, which the check now counts. The third found a sort slip in the","+new check itself. The sequence of fixes is in","+`tests/test_obstruction_minor.py::test_checker_accepts_deletion_of_a_contracted_component`.","+The search module's own quotient code had none of these: its branch sets","+are keyed by surviving representatives and the deleted ones simply leave.","+","+### 4.2 Numbers","+","+**The family closes every one of the 251** (`tables.md` (a), (c)). The","+search's floor equals the optimum on **251 of 251**; the ladder's on 222","+(88.4%), one below on the other 29. The record before this item (`floor0`,","+the best of `lb_best`, `tw + 1`, Harper at cap 12, Lemma P and the file-backed","+minors) was tight on 70 of the 251 and family E's exact floor after item 03","+on 8; `tw + 1` alone on 67, `lb_best` and the clique bound on 0. On the 55","+instances where `floor0` is 2 or more below the optimum (46 by 2, 8 by 3, 1","+by 4), the ladder alone closes 53 and the search the other 2. The search's","+floor is above `floor0` on 181 of the 251 and above the harness's reference","+`max(lb_best, tw + 1)` on 184; through the harness's validity stage on all","+6,376 corpus instances it is **above the optimum on 0** (`harness_table.md`;","+the candidate is a lookup of the run's certificates, 1 elsewhere, as item","+03's was).","+","+| band | instances | ladder tight | search tight | search > ladder | `floor0` tight | family E tight |","+|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|","+| 9–20 | 17 | 12 | 17 | 5 | 4 | — |","+| 21–30 | 133 | 115 | 133 | 18 | 47 | — |","+| 31–40 | 47 | 42 | 47 | 5 | 13 | — |","+| 41–60 | 54 | 53 | 54 | 1 | 6 | — |","+| all | 251 | 222 | 251 | 29 | 70 | 8 |","+","+**Where the search beats the ladder** ((b)): 29 of 251 (11.6%), always by","+exactly one stack and always to the optimum; 14 Harvey, 10 Simonis, 4","+Faggioli–Bentivoglio, 1 Chu & Stuckey (`Random-40-40-4-2_0`); 5 at 20","+customers, 18 at 30, 5 at 40, 1 at 50. In every case the ladder's 95% point","+(at 20 customers, one contraction) fails to prove `optimum − 1` on the","+minor while the search's minor, of the same size or up to 9 vertices larger","+(median 2), does — the greedy choice of *which* edge to contract is what","+the ladder gets wrong, not the size. **Never the other way**: the search's","+floor is below the ladder's on 0 instances (its restarts contain the","+ladder's 50–95% points).","+","+**The minimal certifying minor** ((d)). Over the 251 the search's smallest","+minor at the optimum has `m / n` median 0.66 (IQR 0.52–0.77), against the","+ladder's first certifying point at 0.80 (0.70–0.90; the ladder reaches the","+optimum first at 95% on 43 instances, 85% on 37, 80% on 32, 50% on 12).","+By band the median falls with `n`: 0.75, 0.70, 0.55, 0.51 at 9–20, 21–30,","+31–40, 41–60; it rises with the excess (0.55, 0.62, 0.80 across excess","+terciles; Pearson 0.68 with the realised excess, 0.82 with the graph","+density, 0.88 with `optimum / n`, −0.53 with `n`). The minor is never","+smaller than the optimum plus 2 vertices (median `m − optimum` 7,","+`m / optimum` 1.48), as it cannot be: a graph on `m` vertices has pathwidth","+at most `m − 1`. Every one of the 251 floors is a C `refutation` on the","+minor (0 by the C's `bound`, 0 by its printed `lower`); of the 2,155 ladder","+points 1,523 were refutations, 378 met the C's degeneracy bound and 254 were","+skipped by the lifted-witness rule. The ladder's best point came from","+`min-d` on 235 instances and `least-c` on 16.","+","+**Checker verdicts** ((e)): **251 of 251 verified, all three checks**","+(replay and hash, the C re-proof, and the rule-free `vsmemo` + `checkF`","+refutation of `optimum − 2` on the minor: median 0.14 s, maximum 0.15 s;","+the minors have 12–40 vertices). So every floor this item reports rests on","+minor monotonicity and an 80-line checker, not on the search rules.","+","+**Cost** ((f)): the ladder used **0.007 core-hours** on the 251 (median 5–9","+C calls per instance, 0.0–0.1 s); the search used its whole budget, **5.08","+core-hours**, of which 1.02 in the C program (951,248 calls, median 21.5","+per second, each a process start on a 12–40-vertex graph) and the rest in","+the Python moves (median 6,900 per second, 608 skipped candidates per","+second). The budgets are \"the same total seconds\" in the sense the item","+asks; the ladder needs a hundredth of them. Validation 0.3, the checker","+sweeps 0.03, the harness 0.05, the two restarts' redone instances about","+0.2: **≈ 5.7 core-hours** against the item's 8.","+","+### 4.3 Kill verdict and what this does not claim","+","+**Kill criterion (plan §0.9 M): not met**, by a small margin. The search","+beats the ladder on 29 of 251, 11.6%, against the 10% that would have","+recorded \"greedy is enough at `n ≤ 60`\". The honest reading is narrower","+than the number: the ladder closes 222 and is never more than one stack","+short, and where the search wins it wins by one, at the minor sizes the","+ladder already visits, by choosing a different contraction. The family's","+duality gap on the 338 at `n ≤ 60` is **zero**: exact on all 251, with the","+certificates on disk. The stop conditions did not fire: no minor's C-proved","+width exceeded brute force (1,485 of 1,485), and no certificate was","+rejected by a correct checker (the 5 rejections of the second sweep were","+the checker's, §4.1). Item 05 runs the search on the 87 larger instances","+of the 338 and the 200 Chu & Stuckey, where the ladder is known to miss.","+","+**What this does not claim.** That the search is optimal among contraction","+minors, or that the minimal minor it reports is the smallest certifying","+minor (a search's failure to shrink further is not a proof); that a C","+`refutation` on a minor is independent of the search rules (it rests on","+the corrected rules proved sound in Lean; the rule-free `vsmemo` + `checkF`","+check is the independent one, and here it ran on all 251 because the","+minors are small — it does not scale to the 87-vertex minors of the record,","+which took 255 s and 19.7 GB there); that the 11.6% would hold at larger","+sizes or other budgets (the search spent its whole 60–120 s and the ladder","+0.1 s, so at equal *spent* time the ladder is the better use of a second;","+a search given the ladder's time would evaluate a few dozen candidates);","+that the `m / n` figures describe anything but this search's minima under","+this evaluator (ties by fewer vertices; cap 2 s); any solver change (the C","+program's minor step and `relaxation.py` are untouched). The comparison with","+family E uses item 03's `floor_after` where it exists and item 02's / item","+01's cap-12 floor elsewhere; family E's ceiling is below the optimum on","+most of these instances (item 02), so its 8 tight instances are a property","+of the family, not of its search. \"We found no prior report\" of a local","+search over contraction sequences for pathwidth lower bounds on MOSP","+instances; the ladder is Chu & Stuckey's contraction relaxa