{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","id":"msg_011CgfNtxEwQ7X81QKF9eHbs","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Item 04 is done, the gate passed, and nothing is left running.\n\n**What was done.** Family M (contraction minors) now has a local search over contraction sequences (`learning/obstruction_minor.py`), a certificate format, and an independent `check-minor` in `paper1/obstruction_check.py` that replays with its own code, rebuilds the quotient from branch sets, re-runs the C program and runs the rule-free `vsmemo` + `checkF` refutation. Validation before the run: 1,485 minors on 50 small instances agree with brute force, and the six recorded certificates replay and re-prove at exactly their recorded widths.\n\n**Findings on the 251 bound-gap instances at 20–50 customers.**\n- The family's duality gap is zero: the search's floor equals the optimum on all 251. The greedy ladder is tight on 222 and one stack short on 29. The record before this item was tight on 70, family E on 8.\n- The search beats the ladder on 29 of 251 (11.6%), always by one and always to the optimum, by choosing a different contraction at a size the ladder already visits. The kill criterion (\"greedy is enough\" below 10%) is therefore not met, by a small margin, and the report says the ladder costs a hundredth of the search's time.\n- Minimal certifying minors have median m/n of 0.66 against the ladder's 0.80, shrinking with size and growing with the excess.\n- All 251 certificates verify on all three checks; the harness reports 0 floors above an optimum on the whole corpus.\n\n**Two bugs surfaced, both in the checker, none in a certificate.** Its partition check first crashed on isolated-vertex deletions, then wrongly rejected 5 certificates in which a whole component had been contracted to one vertex and then deleted. Both are fixed with a regression test, and the three attempts' logs are kept.\n\n**Compute:** about 5.6 core-hours of the item's 8. The run was paused and resumed twice to follow the load rule while the owner's chrome processes pushed the load to 59; this is recorded in the run log and the report.\n\nPROGRESS.md has the iteration entry (now 4/11 solved) and the item is marked done in iterations.md. Nothing was committed. Next is item 05, the same search on the 87 larger gap instances and the 200 Chu & Stuckey instances, where the rule-free check will stop fitting above roughly 90-vertex minors."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1437,"cache_read_input_tokens":264260,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1437,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9f928aeb-dd8b-4eb2-ae60-0ddf3b071136","uuid":"4f1e8d0b-071f-419a-bb99-a8f0c36f6dc9","timestamp":"2026-11-03T04:39:46.875Z","request_id":"req_011CgfNtws7p5wUpsBp6h2D5"}
